    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-6429-1",
        "name": "USN-6429-1",
        "description": "Jay Satiro discovered that curl incorrectly handled hostnames when using a SOCKS5 proxy. In environments where curl is configured to use a SOCKS5 proxy, a remote attacker could possibly use this issue to execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 23.04. (CVE-2023-38545)  It was discovered that curl incorrectly handled cookies when an application duplicated certain handles. A local attacker could possibly create a cookie file and inject arbitrary cookies into subsequent connections. (CVE-2023-38546)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2023-38545",
          "CVE-2023-38546"
        ]
      },
      "timestamp": "2023-10-11T11:34:51Z",
